---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  eyebrow="This site"
  text="How This Site Is"
  accent="Built"
  description="Claude Code wrote the code for pa-tech.dev. The constraints I set for it, how tests enforce them, and what the pages weigh as a result."
>
  <p>
    Claude Code, Anthropic's coding agent, wrote the code for this site. I set
    the constraints it works under, reviewed every change and made the
    decisions. This page lists those constraints and how they are enforced.
  </p>

  <h2>Who does what</h2>
  <p>
    Claude Code writes the code and the tests. I define each change as an issue,
    set the rules in the repository's instruction files, review and merge every
    pull request, and make the decisions recorded in the architecture decision
    records.
  </p>

  <h2>The constraints</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      No JavaScript by default. Native HTML and CSS come first, such as{" "}
      <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>, <code>popover</code> and{" "}
      <code>&lt;details&gt;</code>. A script only enhances a native element when
      HTML and CSS cannot do the job.
    </li>
    <li>
      No layout shift. Every image has a set width and height, and the font
      never swaps in late. A test loads a blog post with a slow font and checks
      that nothing moves.
    </li>
    <li>
      A strict Content Security Policy. Every inline script and style is allowed
      by its hash, with no <code>unsafe-inline</code>. A test fails if any page
      breaks the policy.
    </li>
    <li>
      Accessibility checked against WCAG 2.2 AA and the ARIA Authoring Practices
      Guide. Every page is scanned with axe, and keyboard focus, contrast and
      reduced motion have their own tests.
    </li>
    <li>
      Small, reviewed changes. One issue per change and one pull request per
      issue, sized so I can review it in one sitting.
    </li>
    <li>
      Tests in three browsers. Playwright runs the built site in Chromium,
      Firefox and WebKit.
    </li>
    <li>
      Decisions on record. Choices such as the move to Astro are written down as
      architecture decision records.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The result</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No page downloads a JavaScript file.</li>
    <li>
      A blog post loads in about 65&nbsp;KB. The median mobile home page weighs
      2,559&nbsp;KB, 632&nbsp;KB of it JavaScript (
      <a href="https://almanac.httparchive.org/en/2025/page-weight">
        2025 Web Almanac
      </a>
      ).
    </li>
    <li>No layout shift on a throttled mobile connection.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Built with</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>, plain CSS and Markdown, hosted on
    statichost.eu. The code, issues and pull requests are public on{" "}
    <a href="https://github.com/Alexits93/ai-architecture-portfolio">GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
